  "sale_events": [],
  "body": "This family home on one of Mission Bay's best addresses is such a great offering on today's market. Originally built in the 1930's, our owners have enjoyed living here but are now spending more time up north.\r\n\r\nMaking the most of the sea and Rangitoto views, your open-plan kitchen, dining, and lounge room flows out to the large, covered deck (courtesy of the fixed louvre system), doubling the size of your internal living space. All-day sunshine and natural light flood into the home from morning to sunset. Three large bedrooms - master with an ensuite and a family bathroom complete the upstairs floor plan. Downstairs, there are many 'flexi' areas to enjoy - adaptability for a fourth bedroom, a study, workshops, a teenage hang-out space, and generous storage - plus your double internal-access garage. With ample off-street parking and a carport, out the front is the perfect platform from which to extend the home and create something really special on this 870sqm site.\r\n\r\nSurrounded by stunning homes in all directions, you are seriously in great company on one of Mission Bay's top streets.\r\n\r\n* Freehold\r\n\r\n* Floor Area: 210sqm (approx.)\r\n\r\n* Land Area: 870sqm (more or less)\r\n\r\n* Council Rates: $9,289.79 p/a (2026/27)\r\n\r\n* CV: $3,200,000 (2024)\r\n\r\n* School Zones: Kohimarama School, Selwyn College, Baradene College\r\n\r\n* Residential - Single House Zone\r\n\r\nPlease call JAYNE KIELY 021 352 007 or AMY ROBERTSON 0274 820 100\r\n\r\nWe work with all agencies. Conjunctions are welcome.",
